python — Use BAML from Python via a generated Pydantic v2 SDK.

Syntax:
  pip install baml_bridge                  # the runtime (Python 3.10+)
  
  # baml.toml — declare a generator:
  [generator.app]
  output_type = "python/pydantic"        # or "python/pydantic/v1"
  output_dir  = "../app"
  naming_convention = "language"         # snake_case functions and fields
  
  baml generate                          # emits the `baml_sdk` package into output_dir

You install `baml_bridge` (the runtime); you import `baml_sdk` (the generated
code). Functions become top-level Python functions; classes/enums become
Pydantic models. Each function is async; its blocking twin ends in `_sync`:

  import baml_sdk                       # initializes the BAML runtime
  from baml_sdk import classify_ticket, classify_ticket_sync

  async def main():
      ticket = await classify_ticket("login is broken")   # typed in, typed Pydantic out

  ticket = classify_ticket_sync("login is broken")        # same call, blocking

See also: `baml describe baml_sdk`, `baml describe typescript`.
